// Registry 882: a typo in a CAPITALIZED name used to pass `nova check` green and
// detonate at build as [INTERNAL-PANIC] [E_CODEGEN_TYPE_UNKNOWN] `Ident ... not
// in var_types / not a sum-variant`. A typo in a lowercase name was refused
// honestly all along -- so the compiler judged the same mistake by the case of
// its letters.
//
// The cause was an escape hatch in the name-resolution pass that waved through
// EVERY identifier starting with a capital, and its own comment gave the reason:
// bootstrap had no cross-file name resolution. That reason expired with Plan
// 42.15 (per-group declarations, per-peer imports), and the hatch outlived it.
// It is now narrowed to the shape the rationale names -- UpperCamelCase for
// types, variants and modules -- while SCREAMING_SNAKE (a constant, 210 of 211
// in std) must be found for real.
// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR undefined identifier `MAX_SIZ`
module neg.undefined_screaming_ident_neg

const MAX_SIZE = 64

fn main() Io -> () {
    // nova:expect undefined identifier -- one letter short of MAX_SIZE
    println(MAX_SIZ)
}
